WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-database (45s) Narrator Osato

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.815
First, most software burns needless time and power unpacking text and recalculating answers it already solved.

2
00:00:08.255 --> 00:00:15.830
Second, fingerprint-chained logs and dual-time indexes let any machine replay exact past states without guesswork.

3
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:23.893
Third, zero-copy memory-mapped lookup stores turn repeated work into sub-microsecond reads under two microjoules.

4
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:29.669
Instead of unpacking verbose text buffers and recalculating totals on every single click,

5
00:00:29.669 --> 00:00:36.623
a memory-mapped store writes verified answers once in clean binary layout and jumps straight to that memory address.

6
00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:42.088
Pairing fingerprint-chained state logs with sub-microsecond zero-copy memory reads

7
00:00:42.088 --> 00:00:46.806
lets machines remember proven work identically across every operating system.
